course: dictionary
lesson: 11959
title: Context clues: casino
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A casino is a building where people play games of chance, such as cards and roulette, for money. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «The man lost all his savings at the casino.» Savings are money, and losing money in a building full of games tells you a casino is a place where people gamble.
explain: «Only adults are allowed into the casino, so Jo had to wait outside.» The clue is adults: a casino is for grown-ups, because the games are played for money. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Casino can also mean a card game, also spelt cassino. «The family played casino after supper» tells you it is a game played with cards, not a building. The words around a word decide which meaning is right.
fact: A casino is a building where people play games of chance for money.
fact: A game of chance is decided mostly by luck, like the spin of a roulette wheel.
fact: Casinos are only for adults, because gambling for money is not allowed for children.
fact: Probability is the chance of something happening. Casino games are set up so that the casino usually wins over many games.
fact: The phrase «the house always wins» means the casino usually makes more money than it pays out over time, even if some people win on a single night.
exercise: «The casino was full of bright lights and the clatter of coins.» What is a casino? | A shop that sells playing cards | *A building where people play games of chance for money | A library full of books | A park with swings and slides
exercise: «Only adults are allowed into the casino.» Why can children not go in? | Because casinos are always empty | *Because games are played for money and it is for grown-ups | Because casinos are closed at weekends | Because the food there is too spicy
exercise: Maths lesson: why does the casino usually win over many games? | Casinos give away all their money to players | Casinos only play games with dice | Luck never matters at all in a casino | *Probability means the odds are set in the casino's favour
test: «They played casino with a shuffled pack of cards.» In this sentence, casino means: | *a card game | a bus station | a building where people gamble | a kind of cake
test: The phrase «the house always wins» means: | people who play always go home rich | the house is always painted red | the casino gives free money to everyone | *the casino usually makes more money than it pays out over time
exam: Dan says, «The house always wins, so I will never gamble.» What does the phrase «the house always wins» mean? | *The casino usually makes more money than it pays out over time | Every game in a casino is won by the house on the first turn | Dan is the house and always wins | The casino always loses its money to players
